  m_Name: Sibayla
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCInfoSO
  npcID: fray_sibyla
  displayName: Fray Sibyla
  characterFullName: Hernando de la Sibyla
  alias: None
  characterCategory: Clergy / Dominican Friar
  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5c10deae04182a74a86e30f4a4a4a17b, type: 3}
  description: A refined and intelligent Dominican friar known for speaking carefully
    and arguing through precise distinctions. Although outwardly polite, he closely
    observes the people and conflicts around him.
  biography: "Fray Sibyla is a young Dominican friar serving as the curate of Binondo.
    He formerly taught at the Colegio de San Juan de Letran and earned a reputation
    as a highly skilled dialectician. During the gathering, he says little but listens
    carefully and directs questions toward Fray D\xE1maso concerning his transfer
    from San Diego. When the argument between D\xE1maso and Lieutenant Guevara intensifies,
    Sibyla intervenes using elaborate distinctions designed to calm the dispute without
    directly condemning his fellow friar."
  characterFacts:
  - He belongs to the Dominican order.
  - He serves as the curate of Binondo.
  - He formerly taught at the Colegio de San Juan de Letran.
  - He is known as an accomplished dialectician.
  - He is described as youthful, handsome, graceful and polished.
  - He carefully weighs his words before speaking.
  introductionLines:
  - I am Fray Sibyla, a Dominican and the curate of Binondo.
  - I prefer to consider my words carefully before speaking.
  repeatDialogues:
  - lines:
    - One must distinguish carefully before passing judgment.
    - Things are rarely as simple as they first appear.
  - lines:
    - ...
